    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="1389" n="1275" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt and Prime Minister Churchill to the
                        Commander in Chief, Allied Force Headquarters</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Eisenhower</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-08">September 8, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From President and Prime Minister to General Eisenhower, Algiers.</p>
                <p>We agree with line you are taking as indicated in your 387<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d615-f1"/> and are withholding all announcements here and in London
                    until we know what you have said and done.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d615-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Churchill</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d615-f1" n="1" xml:id="d615-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d615-f2" n="2" xml:id="d615-f2-content">
                <p>Eisenhower broadcast his announcement of the armistice (see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1267">p. 1267</ref>) at 6:30
                    p.m., Algiers time, September 8, 1943. See Garland and Smyth, p. 508. A draft of
                    this telegram, in Leahy’s handwriting, signed by Roosevelt and initialed by
                    Churchill, is in the Roosevelt Papers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
